  message: "DONE — PR merged, dev @ 63f90c0827 (rebase merge, GitHub/Woodpecker green; 2041 passed, all changed sources 100% cov).\n\nIMPLEMENTED (the filed recipe, both shapes): the L3 walker now resolves a Subscript over a module-level or function-local dict display (LEGB, nearest binding scope wins) to the union of its literal string values, indexing per-position for tuple-unpack targets. Wired at the assignment form AND the bare 'edge_type=MAP[k]' kwarg site (added for coherence — gate coverage must not depend on whether the producer bound a local first). New helpers: _binding_index / _resolve_dict_literal / _dict_string_values / _resolve_subscript_values; _resolve_function_local gained an optional tree param. The key is deliberately NOT resolved — every value the map can yield is a candidate, the sound over-approximation for a gate.\n\nCONSERVATIVE POSTURE PRESERVED (as the item required): one non-literal map value, a starred unpack target, a value tuple shorter than the unpack index, a non-Name subscript base, or an empty map = silent skip. Never a partial candidate set (which would let the gate report 'clean' on a map whose unresolvable branch is the one shipping the bad value). 17 new tests, producer_coherence.py at 100%.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (the item's own acceptance criterion): a synthetic emitter using the exact WI-rorul shape — handler_suffix, edge_type = _CALL_TYPE_MAP[call_type] with unregistered otp_call/otp_cast — is now FLAGGED by the gate (test_tuple_unpack_from_dict_subscript_resolves_by_position). RED before, GREEN after. The direct 'et = MAP[k]' form likewise.\n\n*** THE FILED 'ZERO CURRENT EXPLOITER' PREMISE WAS FALSE — the hardening found a real leak on its first run. *** find_symbol_kind_producer_violations flagged Symbol.kind='scalar' at hypergumbo-lang-common/graphql.py:155, emitted via _process_graphql_tree's type_kinds dict. It is the SOLE unregistered member of a six-way sibling set — type/input/interface/enum/union are all registered language_construct. The cause is self-referential and worth recording: the corpus enumeration audit-findings 0007 was built from could not see dict-indirected kind= emits at all, so 'scalar' was structurally invisible for exactly as long as the walker was blind to MAP[k]. The gate that would have caught it was the gate that could not see it.\n\nDISPOSITION: registered, not folded. 'scalar Date' is its own GraphQL type-system construct, and 'type' is already taken by object_type_definition in that same dict — conflating them would fuse two distinct constructs (ADR-0027 apex/peer). Follows the mutation/subscription precedent (same analyzer, same audit-omission cause, same 'registered per id-format:F3' shape). Not a contested vocabulary fork, so it landed in this PR rather than a split one: the live-tree gate test_no_strict_producer_violations_for_symbol_kind goes red until it is resolved, so hardening and disposition are coupled by construction — the same 'closing a hole forces green' pattern as WI-nuduv's ratchet surfacing a 6th offender.\n\nCOLLATERAL (all shrink-only / additive): spec §6 registry count corrected 143 -> 152 (it had drifted independently of this change); schema.json + concept-axes.md regenerated (one x-axis-of-values entry each); .ci/schema-coverage-baseline.json picks up 'scalar' (the 4-substrate corpus has no GraphQL files — the pt.22 fourth-artifact lesson) and sheds 29 DEAD entries left behind by the pt.31/pt.32 endpoint_shape prune. No toleration loosened, no SCHEMA_VERSION bump (additive annotation on an open enum; the ast_call_ufcs precedent).\n\nDOCUMENTED RESIDUAL (advance-not-hide): f-string segment expansion still resolves without the module tree, so 'part = MAP[k]; f\"ast_{part}\"' stays unexpandable — conservative, invents no candidate, locked by test_fstring_segment_over_dict_subscript_stays_unexpanded."  # f3ab
